<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01955</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ae318a5d-5c45-4651-b1cc-293e9d3d8ba0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Here are graphs that represent three quadratic functions, defined by:</para>
<para>\(f(x)=x^2-4\)</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Coordinate plane with 3 quadratic functions. Curve A opens up and has minimum at 0 comma 4. Curve B opens up and has minimum at negative 4 comma 0. Curve C opens down and has maximum 0 comma 1."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1315d2846792f9c61cb68b722d2e7a89c489119b"/></media></figure></para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="723c1300-c3d6-46ff-872c-1d7a5f5f1fd4" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;

  <!--Q#-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="200d8791-5375-4d74-8a94-8d7d0b9bad61" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Blue Graph B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Green Graph A&quot;, &quot;Blue Graph B&quot;, &quot;Black Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph represents the equation \(f(x)=x^2-4\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Blue Graph B because the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-4)\) and the graph opens upward.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#2-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="cd497fb3-7b75-4099-a3c2-2278ada45ded" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Black Graph C" data-solution-options="[&quot;Green Graph A&quot;, &quot;Blue Graph B&quot;, &quot;Black Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph represents the equation \(g(x)=1-x^2\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Black Graph C because the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,1)\) and the graph opens downward.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;<!--Q#3-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="5007f1e3-3da1-4798-a4ba-f8447ef38153" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Green Graph A" data-solution-options="[&quot;Green Graph A&quot;, &quot;Blue Graph B&quot;, &quot;Black Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph represents the equation \(h(x)=x^2+4\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Green Graph A because the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,4)\) and the graph opens upward.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
